[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:On Strike]
[00:01.36]Who will be driving the buses next week? | 下周谁来开公交车？
[00:14.23]Busmen have decided to go on strike next week. | 公交车司机们已决定下周举行罢工。
[00:19.35]The strike is due to begin on Tuesday. | 罢工定于周二开始。
[00:23.38]No one knows how long it will last. | 没人知道罢工会持续多久。
[00:27.10]The busmen have stated that the strike will continue until general agreement is reached about pay and working conditions. | 公交车司机们声明，罢工将持续到在工资和工作条件方面达成普遍协议为止。
[00:37.54]Most people believe that the strike will last for at least a week. | 大多数人认为罢工至少会持续一周。
[00:43.66]Many owners of private cars are going to offer 'free rides' to people on their way to work. | 许多私家车车主将为上班族提供“免费搭车”服务。
[00:51.52]This will relieve pressure on the trains to some extent. | 这将在一定程度上减轻火车的压力。
[00:56.39]Meanwhile, a number of university students have volunteered to drive buses while the strike lasts. | 同时，一些大学生已志愿在罢工期间驾驶公交车。
[01:05.02]All the students are expert drivers, | 所有学生都是驾驶专家，
[01:08.61]but before they drive any of the buses, they will have to pass a special test. | 但在他们驾驶任何公交车之前，他们必须通过一项特殊的考试。
[01:15.90]The students are going to take the test in two days' time. | 学生们将在两天后参加考试。
[01:21.19]Even so, people are going to find it difficult to get to work. | 即使如此，人们仍然会发现上班很困难。
[01:27.08]But so far, the public has expressed its gratitude to the students in lettters to the Press. | 但到目前为止，公众已通过写信给报社的方式表达了对学生的感激之情。
[01:34.82]Only one or two people have objected that the students will drive too fast! | 只有一两个人反对，认为学生们会开得太快！